Task 4.4,4.4_Llama_Socratic_Method.json,Task_Maths_4.4.2_LLAMA_socratic_method,4.4,Llama,,Socratic_Method,llama-3.2-1b-instruct.gguf,13,user,No.,,,,,,,,not_applicable
Task 4.4,4.4_Llama_Socratic_Method.json,Task_Maths_4.4.2_LLAMA_socratic_method,4.4,Llama,,Socratic_Method,llama-3.2-1b-instruct.gguf,14,assistant,Does adding tenths and hundredths add up to the same value as adding just a single digit in the decimal column (tens or ones place)?,1,0,1,0,0,0,"The response contains a factual contradiction. The question states 'adding tenths and hundredths add up to the same value as adding just a single digit in the decimal column (tens or ones place).' This is mathematically incorrect. Tenths and hundredths are decimal place values (to the right of the decimal point), while tens and ones are whole number place values (to the left of the decimal point). These are fundamentally different positional values and do not represent equivalent magnitudes. For example, 0.1 (one tenth) + 0.01 (one hundredth) = 0.11, which is not equal to any single digit in the tens or ones place. The premise of the question contradicts established mathematical facts about place value.",completed
