Task 4.7,4.7_Llama_Socratic_Method.json,Task4.7_llama_Socratic,4.7,Llama,,Socratic_Method,llama-3.2-1b-instruct.gguf,10,assistant,"Teacher: Can you re-examine your addition of 2.6 to 1.35, and how you can break down each number into its tens and hundreds place values?",0,0,1,0,0,0,"The response asks the student to break down 2.6 and 1.35 into 'tens and hundreds place values.' This is mathematically incorrect. The number 2.6 has only a ones place (2) and a tenths place (0.6); it has no tens or hundreds place. Similarly, 1.35 has a ones place (1), tenths place (0.3), and hundredths place (0.05); it has no tens or hundreds place. The instruction to decompose these decimal numbers by tens and hundreds places contradicts established mathematical place value definitions.",completed
